# large run artefacts: keep configs, logs, scores; drop weights/renders/clouds.
# The point clouds and Gaussian checkpoints are published on Hugging Face at
# manishjoshiai/twinworld2026-verification; they do not belong in git, and the
# individual files run to several hundred megabytes each, well past GitHub's
# 100 MB limit.
experiments/**/renders/
experiments/**/ckpt/
experiments/**/*.ply
experiments/**/*.pth
experiments/**/*.npz
experiments/**/*.pt
experiments/**/*.tar
experiments/**/*.png
submissions/
*.zip

# 68k flat run logs, 273 MB. The curated record of what every run showed is
# docs/PROGRESS.md; these are the raw stdout behind it and are not worth
# versioning.
logs/

# Scraped Codabench state. These dumps carry 26 other participants' user names
# and at least one third party's personal e-mail address, which are not ours to
# republish. Git history is permanent, so they stay out from the first commit
# rather than being removed before going public.
docs/competition/

# Working notes, not part of the released work.
docs/superpowers/
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/GPU_HANDBACK.md
docs/UPLOAD_LADDER.md
docs/FINAL_PHASE.md
